Decide whether the supplied new subject node is the same subject as one already found earlier in this batch.

A subject node groups references to one subject in the current batch. A local identity is a subject found earlier in
this same batch that did not match the stored registry.

Return `same_as_local` only when the evidence establishes one exact local identity through its name and defining
context. Otherwise return `distinct`. Similar topics, shared participants, or apparent type do not establish identity.
This step does not revisit stored identities or decide type, page visibility, containment, or claim ownership. Return
one schema-valid decision for the supplied node ID.
